<title>CANADA: Wajax acquires Spencer Industries.</title>
<headline>Wajax acquires Spencer Industries.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wajax Ltd said on Thursday it completed the first U.S. expansion initiative in its strategic acquisition program by acquiring Spencer Industries, a Seattle-based multi-line distributor of hydraulics and related components.</p>
<p>Financial details of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Wajax said Spencer's annual sales were about US$40 million and continuing growth was anticipated due to the recent expansion of Spencer's U.S. branch network.</p>
<p>Spencer has 11 branches in the western United States and three branches in British Columbia and Alberta.</p>
<p>Wajax said it was pursuing further strategic acquisition opportunities to expand its industrial components business and the distribution and servicing of mobile equipment and diesel engines.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
